   "id": "c2",
   "kind": "concept",
   "body": "Each output component is a **row of the matrix dotted with the vector** (recall the dot product). The top row makes the new x; the bottom row makes the new y. A matrix is a machine that recombines a vector's coordinates by fixed recipes — the rows.",
   "figure": "vec-matrix-row-dot"
  },
